# rrubocop

10x faster RuboCop drop-in for Ruby (tree-sitter). Same CLI, configs, and output — no RuboCop gems to maintain.

## Layout
- `src/cli.rs` — RuboCop-compatible CLI
- `src/baseline.rs` + `src/resources/baseline.json` — RuboCop/gem versions for `--help`/`--version`
- `src/config/` — RuboCop-parity YAML (`mod.rs` re-exports; `gem_path`, `yaml_read` ERB (native simple-ERB: literals/vars/`ENV`; ruby fallback), `types`, `globutil`, `filter`/`filter_match`/`filter_path`, `discover`, `standard`/`standard_convert`, `merge`/`merge_cop`, `parse`/`parse_{allcops,cop}`, `load`/`load_{defaults,require,gems,recursive,lockfile,resolve}`, `ruby_ver`, `resolved`/`resolved_{state,enabled,inject,cop_cfg,filters,effective,fingerprint}`)
- `src/cache/` — abcop-style redb result cache (`RRUBOCOP_CACHE_DIR` / XDG)
- `src/cop/` — cops by department (`bundler`, `factory_bot`(+association_style), `gemspec`(+ordered_dependencies_group), `graphql`(+helpers/{args,kwargs,description,names_field,klass,names}; 26 cops), `layout` (90 Layout cops), `lint` (66), `metrics`, `naming`, `performance`, `rails`, `rake`, `rspec`(+helpers), `rspec_rails`(+inferred_spec_type), `security`, `style` (143 Style cops + `heuristics/` {percent,string_literals,…} + `trailing_comma_args`), `shared`, `walker`, `registry`)
- `src/fs.rs` — file discover; `AllCops.Exclude` via CopFilterSet (RuboCop `-L`)
- `src/parse/` — SourceFile, CodeMap, directives, tree-sitter parse
- `src/linter/` — parallel lint + cache (`mod.rs`, `parallel.rs`) and per-file phases (`engine/` + `syntax_gate`); line/source opt-in, shared `FileModel` for variable/metrics cops, single AST `BatchedWalker` by `interested_node_kinds`
- `src/formatter/` — text/json/progress (live marks)/…
- `src/abc/`, `src/model/` — Metrics/AbcSize (tree-sitter)
- `vendor/tree-sitter-ruby/` — grammar
- `testdata/cross_test_nitrocop.py` — offense compare vs local nitrocop
- `tests/fixtures/cops/` — nitrocop-style `offense.rb` / `no_offense.rb` per cop (`src/testutil/` + `cop_fixture_tests!`); when fixing FPs/parity, always add fixtures (see `.cursor/rules/cop-parity-tests.mdc`)
- Reference clones (outside repo): `/home/crexus/nitrocop`, `/home/crexus/rubocop`, `/home/crexus/abcop`
- Parity on external projects: compare against `bundle exec rubocop` (project Gemfile), not bare `rubocop` from PATH — see `.cursor/rules/cop-parity-tests.mdc`
- CI (`ci.yml`): `cargo test --locked` + [abcop](https://github.com/adrianov/abcop) `--full` (pinned `.deb` from Releases; AbcSize ≤17 / ModuleAbcSize ≤120; no Rust disable directives — split modules / extract fns)
- Publish (`publish.yml`): tag `v*` → crates.io + Ubuntu 22.04 `.deb` + macOS `.tar.gz` GitHub Release; Homebrew tap `adrianov/rrubocop`
- `.cursor/rules/squash-merge-prs.mdc` — auto squash-merge every ready PR after `ci`, then delete the head branch; `.github/workflows/auto-merge.yml` lands them (do not `gh pr merge --auto` here — no required checks)
